&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

3
00:00:17,213 --> 00:00:19,924
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived, it's here&lt;/i&gt;

4
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:23,010
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

5
00:00:23,219 --> 00:00:25,596
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived, here it is!&lt;/i&gt;

6
00:00:25,805 --> 00:00:28,850
&lt;i&gt;Big waves, small waves,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tiny waves and middle-size waves&lt;/i&gt;

7
00:00:29,058 --> 00:00:31,477
&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

8
00:00:31,686 --> 00:00:34,730
&lt;i&gt;Big boobs, small boobs,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tiny boobs and middle-size boobs&lt;/i&gt;

9
00:00:34,939 --> 00:00:37,733
&lt;i&gt;At the beach&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Jiggle, jiggle, jiggle!&lt;/i&gt;

10
00:00:37,942 --> 00:00:40,736
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

11
00:00:40,945 --> 00:00:43,781
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived, it's here&lt;/i&gt;

12
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:46,576
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

13
00:00:46,784 --> 00:00:49,245
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;it's here already!&lt;/i&gt;

14
00:00:49,454 --> 00:00:52,498
&lt;i&gt;Big waves, small waves,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tiny waves and middle-size waves&lt;/i&gt;

15
00:00:52,707 --> 00:00:55,334
&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

16
00:00:55,543 --> 00:00:58,337
&lt;i&gt;Big butts, small butts,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tiny butts and middle-size butts&lt;/i&gt;

17
00:00:58,546 --> 00:01:02,842
&lt;i&gt;At the beach&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Bounce, bounce, bounce!&lt;/i&gt;

18
00:01:05,928 --> 00:01:14,687
&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

19
00:01:17,815 --> 00:01:21,319
&lt;i&gt;Bouncing at the beach&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Jiggling at the beach&lt;/i&gt;

20
00:01:23,154 --> 00:01:24,197
&lt;i&gt;Want you!&lt;/i&gt;

21
00:01:28,284 --> 00:01:34,040
A VISIT TO THE NAKAGAWA RESIDENCE

22
00:01:35,374 --> 00:01:39,921
Hey, guys. I'm going to order some lunch. What does everyone want?

23
00:01:40,463 --> 00:01:42,757
I'll have pork noodles and dumplings.

24
00:01:42,965 --> 00:01:44,926
I'll have liver and chives, please.

25
00:01:45,343 --> 00:01:47,178
Fried rice for me.

26
00:01:47,762 --> 00:01:48,930
And Ryo-chan?

27
00:01:49,138 --> 00:01:52,183
It's the day before payday, so just ramen and rice, right?

28
00:01:56,395 --> 00:01:58,523
Ryo-chan, what are you doing?

29
00:01:58,731 --> 00:02:00,817
Surely you're not on a diet?

30
00:02:01,025 --> 00:02:04,028
Oh, how silly of me! You'd never do anything like that.

31
00:02:04,362 --> 00:02:06,531
As if I'd go on a diet!

32
00:02:06,739 --> 00:02:10,535
I'm just exercising to make myself hungry, that's all!

33
00:02:10,952 --> 00:02:13,538
Oh? So you're not hungry?

34
00:02:13,746 --> 00:02:15,373
I never said that.

35
00:02:15,581 --> 00:02:18,000
It's for that party tonight at Nakagawa's.

36
00:02:18,584 --> 00:02:20,253
Oh, that's right.

37
00:02:20,670 --> 00:02:24,507
Hey, Nakagawa. You've got some great food planned for tonight, don'tcha?

38
00:02:24,715 --> 00:02:30,346
Absolutely. Several top chefs will be pulling out all the stops.

39
00:02:30,555 --> 00:02:33,307
We don't get to eat food like that often, do we?

40
00:02:34,141 --> 00:02:35,977
So you want to keep room for that?

41
00:02:36,185 --> 00:02:40,231
Damn straight! Not to brag, but I haven't eaten a thing for two days!

42
00:02:40,439 --> 00:02:43,568
You moron. How do you expect to work on an empty stomach?

43
00:02:43,776 --> 00:02:45,361
You should at least eat lunch.

44
00:02:45,570 --> 00:02:51,075
You may be the chief, but you have no right to tell your workers when to eat.

45
00:02:51,492 --> 00:02:56,706
And you. Noodles and dumplings are filling. You sure you wanna eat that?

46
00:02:56,914 --> 00:02:58,791
You'll be too full for the party.

47
00:02:59,292 --> 00:03:00,668
Hmm, you might be right.

48
00:03:01,168 --> 00:03:05,214
Reiko, scratch the dumplings. Just get the pork noodles.

49
00:03:05,423 --> 00:03:06,299
Oh, okay.

50
00:03:06,507 --> 00:03:09,594
Me too. Forget the liver and chives. I'll just have ramen.

51
00:03:10,261 --> 00:03:11,762
Okay, I got it.

52
00:03:23,232 --> 00:03:27,778
Say, Nakagawa. What's this party for, anyway?

53
00:03:28,112 --> 00:03:30,781
It's a birthday party for the Prince of Hondara.

54
00:03:31,407 --> 00:03:32,491
Hondara?

55
00:03:32,992 --> 00:03:35,494
It's a small country. Not many have heard of it.

56
00:03:35,703 --> 00:03:38,914
My father's old friends with their king,

57
00:03:39,123 --> 00:03:42,001
so when they come to Japan, they come and stay with us.

58
00:03:42,209 --> 00:03:44,045
"NAKAGAWA EXIT 500 M"

59
00:03:49,550 --> 00:03:52,762
I've never ridden in such a wide Ferrari before.

60
00:03:52,970 --> 00:03:56,557
I asked the chairman of Ferrari to make me one with a wide body.

61
00:03:57,058 --> 00:03:59,560
Isn't it illegal to take up two lanes like this?

62
00:04:00,186 --> 00:04:03,564
Don't worry. This is a private road owned by the Nakagawa family.

63
00:04:03,773 --> 00:04:05,316
What did you say?

64
00:04:05,524 --> 00:04:08,694
We just turned off at the "Nakagawa Exit."

65
00:04:08,903 --> 00:04:11,072
Don't tell me it's named after your family?

66
00:04:11,530 --> 00:04:14,575
It is. We had that exit made specifically for our house.

67
00:04:15,326 --> 00:04:16,786
Eh?!

68
00:04:17,286 --> 00:04:19,997
More importantly, are we still not there yet?

69
00:04:20,206 --> 00:04:21,749
I'm dying of starvation here.

70
00:04:22,667 --> 00:04:24,502
Well, technically we're here.

71
00:04:24,710 --> 00:04:29,173
What? I don't see any houses here. Just a wall that goes on forever.

72
00:04:29,382 --> 00:04:31,634
That's the wall around our house.

73
00:04:31,842 --> 00:04:32,635
What?!

74
00:04:52,697 --> 00:04:55,157
How large exactly is the property?

75
00:04:55,866 --> 00:04:58,703
Around 100 times the size of Disneyland, I think?

76
00:04:58,911 --> 00:05:00,705
What?!

77
00:05:01,288 --> 00:05:06,460
If it's so big, why don't you have multiple ways of getting in?

78
00:05:07,044 --> 00:05:09,505
The property has 12 entrances in total.

79
00:05:09,714 --> 00:05:14,385
Right now, we're heading for Mitoko Gate, which is the closest one.

80
00:05:15,136 --> 00:05:16,095
Mitoko Gate?

81
00:05:16,595 --> 00:05:21,851
There are others. There's Gaisen Gate, Seishunno Gate, and Kinokuniya Bunzae Gate.

82
00:05:22,351 --> 00:05:24,395
Huh...

83
00:05:36,115 --> 00:05:38,576
Master Keiichi has arrived.

84
00:05:42,288 --> 00:05:44,790
Well, here we are. I'll speed up a little.

85
00:05:53,799 --> 00:05:54,592
Huh?

86
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:55,676
What's wrong?

87
00:05:56,469 --> 00:05:58,053
I think I'm lost.

88
00:06:00,056 --> 00:06:01,724
But this is your property!

89
00:06:01,932 --> 00:06:03,184
I'll turn on the GPS.

90
00:06:04,268 --> 00:06:06,187
&lt;i&gt;Please confirm your destination.&lt;/i&gt;

91
00:06:07,772 --> 00:06:11,817
What sort of person needs a GPS to get around his own property...

92
00:06:15,780 --> 00:06:17,990
Oh, look! There's the house now.

93
00:06:18,491 --> 00:06:20,826
It looks as big as your house, Chief.

94
00:06:21,035 --> 00:06:23,287
Pretty puny on such a big plot.

95
00:06:23,704 --> 00:06:24,663
Excuse me?

96
00:06:25,748 --> 00:06:27,750
I think it's a splendid house.

97
00:06:27,958 --> 00:06:30,753
Sorry to burst your bubble, but that's the doghouse.

98
00:06:32,046 --> 00:06:37,384
So the chief's got a 20-year mortgage on what's essentially a doghouse?

99
00:06:39,678 --> 00:06:41,597
Ryo-san...

100
00:06:45,309 --> 00:06:47,394
You laugh too much.

101
00:06:53,025 --> 00:06:55,903
What... in... the... hell?!

102
00:06:56,654 --> 00:06:58,030
This is your house?

103
00:06:58,239 --> 00:07:02,409
Yes. Well, one of the wings, to be more precise.

104
00:07:02,827 --> 00:07:05,496
My parents live in that house over there.

105
00:07:06,580 --> 00:07:09,291
And my sister lives in that one there.

106
00:07:09,750 --> 00:07:14,213
What humble beginnings you come from.

107
00:07:15,339 --> 00:07:16,298
Come on in.

108
00:07:20,010 --> 00:07:23,138
This is your living room?

109
00:07:23,722 --> 00:07:25,641
Oh! Look at that!

110
00:07:26,433 --> 00:07:28,811
Wow! It's a classic arcade game!

111
00:07:29,019 --> 00:07:31,647
And it's black-and-white with colored cellophane!

112
00:07:33,566 --> 00:07:35,568
This is amazing!

113
00:07:35,776 --> 00:07:36,944
He even has a pool!

114
00:07:37,736 --> 00:07:40,239
Well, that's actually the bathtub.

115
00:07:40,447 --> 00:07:41,657
The pool's over here.

116
00:07:44,743 --> 00:07:46,996
The bathtub is moving?

117
00:07:47,204 --> 00:07:50,541
No, it's this whole room that's moving.

118
00:07:50,749 --> 00:07:51,959
The room?

119
00:07:54,461 --> 00:07:56,630
This beats even amusement park pools.

120
00:07:57,673 --> 00:08:02,303
There's a golf course! And even an airport!

121
00:08:02,511 --> 00:08:04,889
Yes! 50,000 points!

122
00:08:05,097 --> 00:08:09,018
You're no match for my Nagoya Attack!

123
00:08:09,727 --> 00:08:11,186
Let's just ignore him.

124
00:08:14,607 --> 00:08:15,691
What's wrong?

125
00:08:29,788 --> 00:08:31,373
What happened?

126
00:08:55,064 --> 00:08:56,023
May I come in?

127
00:08:56,232 --> 00:08:57,441
Yes, come in.

128
00:09:01,654 --> 00:09:04,156
Reiko-san, that dress looks good on you.

129
00:09:04,365 --> 00:09:05,366
Thanks.

130
00:09:05,574 --> 00:09:09,119
Why do we have to dress in such stuffy clothes?

131
00:09:09,328 --> 00:09:12,915
There'll be a lot of important people at this party.

132
00:09:13,123 --> 00:09:14,166
Just hang in there.

133
00:09:14,750 --> 00:09:19,505
Either way, Ryotsu, you look the same even when you're wearing a tuxedo.

134
00:09:20,339 --> 00:09:22,132
None of your business!

135
00:09:24,051 --> 00:09:25,928
What's happening? An earthquake?!

136
00:09:26,887 --> 00:09:28,347
Everyone, keep calm!

137
00:09:28,681 --> 00:09:34,812
Us police officers must remain calm and collected no matter the circumstances!

138
00:09:36,355 --> 00:09:38,399
It's not an earthquake.

139
00:09:38,607 --> 00:09:39,984
It's just the elevator.

140
00:09:40,317 --> 00:09:43,779
What? You're telling me this entire room is an elevator?

141
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:48,534
So my house is smaller than an elevator, is it?

142
00:09:50,369 --> 00:09:51,537
-Welcome. -Welcome.

143
00:09:59,795 --> 00:10:01,171
Sure are a lot of people.

144
00:10:01,380 --> 00:10:04,633
Oh, look! Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto is here.

145
00:10:04,842 --> 00:10:09,346
And over there is Sara Takaoka from that hair product commercial,

146
00:10:09,555 --> 00:10:12,933
and there's Chief's favorite, Saburo Kitajima!

147
00:10:13,142 --> 00:10:15,144
I'll ask for an autograph later.

148
00:10:16,061 --> 00:10:17,312
Oh man.

149
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:19,857
Now then. Where's the food?

150
00:10:20,733 --> 00:10:21,859
Ryotsu, wait!

151
00:10:23,569 --> 00:10:24,361
What is it?

152
00:10:24,570 --> 00:10:27,489
I'd like to introduce you to the Prince of Hondara.

153
00:10:28,490 --> 00:10:30,617
Hey, Prince Hondara!

154
00:10:32,161 --> 00:10:34,288
Oh, Keiichi!

155
00:10:35,873 --> 00:10:37,207
Happy birthday!

156
00:10:37,416 --> 00:10:38,292
Thank you!

157
00:10:39,418 --> 00:10:45,090
I was expecting a prince charming, but it's just some porky kid.

158
00:10:45,299 --> 00:10:46,341
Ryo-chan!

159
00:10:49,678 --> 00:10:50,554
What is it?

160
00:10:55,267 --> 00:10:58,729
Now, now, Your Highness. Allow me to introduce my coworkers.

161
00:10:59,438 --> 00:11:01,482
This is my boss, Chief Ohara.

162
00:11:01,690 --> 00:11:04,735
Nice to meet you.

163
00:11:05,235 --> 00:11:06,737
And my senior, Ryotsu-san.

164
00:11:08,489 --> 00:11:13,619
Allô, allô! Je t'aime! Ten and ten is twenty, twenty and twenty is forty.

165
00:11:14,870 --> 00:11:17,623
What's this old codger goin' on about?

166
00:11:18,415 --> 00:11:21,085
The prince is fluent in Japanese.

167
00:11:21,293 --> 00:11:23,295
Seriously?! Why didn't you say so?

168
00:11:23,879 --> 00:11:29,426
Behold! I am the man, the one, who will bear Japan into the future!

169
00:11:29,635 --> 00:11:32,262
Kankichi Ryotsu!

170
00:11:34,139 --> 00:11:37,392
This gorilla tells really lame jokes.

171
00:11:37,601 --> 00:11:39,311
Says the little piglet!

172
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:41,688
Who you callin' a piglet?!

173
00:11:41,897 --> 00:11:47,277
Now, now. This is your birthday party, so let's all try to have a good time.

174
00:11:47,486 --> 00:11:52,032
Now that we're done with introductions, I'm getting out of here.

175
00:11:57,704 --> 00:12:01,250
Please pay him no mind, Your Highness. He's just an idiot.

176
00:12:01,834 --> 00:12:04,420
&lt;i&gt;That stupid gorilla!&lt;/i&gt;

177
00:12:11,468 --> 00:12:14,763
Hey, chef. Give me ten plates of tuna and sea urchin sushi.

178
00:12:14,972 --> 00:12:21,145
Sorry, but I'm not to serve food until the prince blows out his birthday candles.

179
00:12:21,353 --> 00:12:24,148
I haven't eaten anything in two days! Help a guy out!

180
00:12:24,356 --> 00:12:25,607
Give him what he wants.

181
00:12:25,816 --> 00:12:26,775
Oh, my Prince!

182
00:12:26,984 --> 00:12:29,153
I will allow it. Let him eat.

183
00:12:29,736 --> 00:12:32,156
Hey, you really are a good little dude.

184
00:12:36,618 --> 00:12:37,494
What is it?

185
00:12:37,703 --> 00:12:42,207
I simply told him to make something extra nice for Keiichi's senior.

186
00:12:42,416 --> 00:12:45,127
Hey, you'll be a great king one day!

187
00:12:45,335 --> 00:12:46,670
Go on, then. Snap snap.

188
00:12:46,879 --> 00:12:47,671
Sure!

189
00:12:48,213 --> 00:12:49,631
Here you go.

190
00:12:51,049 --> 00:12:53,343
Oh, this tuna looks tasty!

191
00:12:56,430 --> 00:12:57,973
Mmm, that's good stuff.

192
00:13:02,269 --> 00:13:05,189
Wasabi!

193
00:13:06,899 --> 00:13:11,195
He fell for it, hook, line, and stinker! That's for insulting me!

194
00:13:11,403 --> 00:13:16,408
And now, ladies and gentlemen, the prince will now blow out the candles!

195
00:13:16,617 --> 00:13:19,203
Your Highness, will you please come this way?

196
00:13:19,411 --> 00:13:20,913
Comin'!

197
00:13:24,750 --> 00:13:27,169
You won't get away with this!

198
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:42,184
Cheeky brats like him need to know their place.

199
00:14:11,213 --> 00:14:12,965
Happy birthday!

200
00:14:13,173 --> 00:14:14,216
Your Highness!

201
00:14:15,759 --> 00:14:16,718
Now!

202
00:14:23,308 --> 00:14:24,893
You missed.

203
00:14:32,985 --> 00:14:35,028
How could you do that to the prince?!

204
00:14:35,237 --> 00:14:36,905
It was just a joke.

205
00:14:37,281 --> 00:14:40,450
&lt;i&gt;You'll regret this, you dumb gorilla!&lt;/i&gt;

206
00:14:44,079 --> 00:14:46,456
Excuse me, Master Keiichi.

207
00:14:46,790 --> 00:14:47,624
What?!

208
00:14:48,375 --> 00:14:51,628
There are intruders at the party?

209
00:14:52,337 --> 00:14:56,633
It looks to be the work of Hondaran dissidents.

210
00:14:56,842 --> 00:14:57,634
That means...

211
00:14:59,261 --> 00:15:00,804
What's wrong, Nakagawa?

212
00:15:01,013 --> 00:15:02,472
Chief, we have a problem.

213
00:15:02,681 --> 00:15:05,142
The prince is being targeted by terrorists.

214
00:15:05,350 --> 00:15:06,143
What?!

215
00:15:07,978 --> 00:15:10,230
All right!

216
00:15:10,439 --> 00:15:13,233
Let's start with some Chinese food.

217
00:15:14,651 --> 00:15:16,069
One of these...

218
00:15:17,696 --> 00:15:19,448
And one of these...

219
00:15:20,907 --> 00:15:22,826
And this...

220
00:15:24,828 --> 00:15:28,582
And this, and this, and this...

221
00:15:33,211 --> 00:15:34,671
Yes, that'll do for now.

222
00:15:38,633 --> 00:15:40,135
Thanks for the grub.

223
00:15:41,678 --> 00:15:45,891
Why you...! Hold it right there!

224
00:15:48,685 --> 00:15:51,438
I'm so hungry I don't even have the energy to run.

225
00:15:55,359 --> 00:15:56,652
Aim carefully this time.

226
00:15:56,860 --> 00:15:57,652
I know.

227
00:16:02,866 --> 00:16:05,410
Let's find those terrorists as soon as possible.

228
00:16:05,619 --> 00:16:06,536
And Ryo-chan?

229
00:16:06,745 --> 00:16:08,789
He wouldn't be of any use anyway.

230
00:16:08,997 --> 00:16:11,875
We have to ensure the safety of the guests first.

231
00:16:12,084 --> 00:16:12,876
-Right. -Right.

232
00:16:17,964 --> 00:16:19,424
I touched it first!

233
00:16:19,633 --> 00:16:21,510
No, I did!

234
00:16:22,010 --> 00:16:23,887
You stand before a prince, sir!

235
00:16:24,096 --> 00:16:26,556
Forget royalty. This is food!

236
00:16:26,765 --> 00:16:28,642
This meat is mine!

237
00:16:37,442 --> 00:16:38,819
Yes! It's mine!

238
00:16:49,371 --> 00:16:50,163
What's wrong?

239
00:16:50,372 --> 00:16:51,581
What happened?

240
00:16:51,790 --> 00:16:55,335
Everyone, you're all in danger! Please get on the ground.

241
00:16:55,544 --> 00:16:57,587
There are terrorists among us!

242
00:17:02,259 --> 00:17:04,428
My meat!

243
00:17:05,178 --> 00:17:07,264
My meat...

244
00:17:07,472 --> 00:17:09,433
That's my meat!

245
00:17:09,933 --> 00:17:11,935
Damn it. Missed again.

246
00:17:12,811 --> 00:17:14,271
Only one way forward.

247
00:17:14,479 --> 00:17:16,565
We go inside and take them all out.

248
00:17:16,940 --> 00:17:17,816
Right.

249
00:17:29,077 --> 00:17:29,953
What's going on?

250
00:17:35,125 --> 00:17:36,793
What is this?

251
00:17:37,252 --> 00:17:38,545
Please remain calm.

252
00:17:38,753 --> 00:17:41,465
The center of the room is simply moving underground.

253
00:17:41,673 --> 00:17:42,466
We'll be safe.

254
00:17:42,799 --> 00:17:44,718
No! My food!

255
00:17:45,302 --> 00:17:48,346
You gotta be kidding! I still haven't eaten anything yet!

256
00:17:51,391 --> 00:17:53,226
-Ryo-chan! -Ryotsu!

257
00:17:53,643 --> 00:17:55,729
Ryo-chan, get down here!

258
00:17:55,937 --> 00:17:57,147
Forget him.

259
00:17:57,355 --> 00:17:59,149
It's the prince they're after.

260
00:17:59,357 --> 00:18:01,234
As long as the prince is safe...

261
00:18:02,611 --> 00:18:05,614
Your Highness!

262
00:18:05,822 --> 00:18:07,782
This could not get any worse.

263
00:18:07,991 --> 00:18:09,993
Hey, let go of me!

264
00:18:10,202 --> 00:18:12,746
I am not letting you eat anything!

265
00:18:15,874 --> 00:18:17,751
You idiot! Stop that!

266
00:18:27,219 --> 00:18:28,845
The last plate!

267
00:18:31,264 --> 00:18:32,724
Still want it?

268
00:18:34,059 --> 00:18:35,852
Come here, you!

269
00:18:41,024 --> 00:18:42,567
&lt;i&gt;Ryotsu! Your Highness!&lt;/i&gt;

270
00:18:42,776 --> 00:18:44,486
&lt;i&gt;Please evacuate immediately!&lt;/i&gt;

271
00:18:45,195 --> 00:18:46,696
I'm busy right now!

272
00:19:02,420 --> 00:19:05,173
Oh, it's my favorite! A whole roast chicken!

273
00:19:05,382 --> 00:19:06,424
What?

274
00:19:06,633 --> 00:19:07,884
I found it first!

275
00:19:08,093 --> 00:19:10,262
It's a dog-eat-dog world, kid!

276
00:19:11,137 --> 00:19:13,223
&lt;i&gt;You moron! This is no time for that!&lt;/i&gt;

277
00:19:13,431 --> 00:19:14,474
&lt;i&gt;They're coming!&lt;/i&gt;

278
00:19:14,683 --> 00:19:16,476
They're here!

279
00:19:18,144 --> 00:19:18,937
Hands up!

280
00:19:21,940 --> 00:19:24,985
You idiot! What did I just say? I'm busy!

281
00:19:29,030 --> 00:19:30,407
Now you've done it!

282
00:19:32,993 --> 00:19:34,786
Don't ignore us!

283
00:19:38,832 --> 00:19:39,624
My chicken!

284
00:19:39,958 --> 00:19:40,750
Damn it!

285
00:19:41,376 --> 00:19:42,878
My roast chicken!

286
00:19:43,712 --> 00:19:46,673
-Hold it right there! -Hey! That's mine!

287
00:19:46,881 --> 00:19:48,967
-Son of a...! -Take us for fools, huh?

288
00:19:54,639 --> 00:19:55,515
I got it!

289
00:19:55,724 --> 00:19:57,058
It's mine!

290
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:03,690
Where's the chicken?

291
00:20:03,898 --> 00:20:04,733
Now!

292
00:20:08,194 --> 00:20:08,987
What the...?

293
00:20:17,621 --> 00:20:20,415
It's sleeping gas. That should be enough.

294
00:20:28,256 --> 00:20:30,175
All right! Time to cuff them.

295
00:20:32,802 --> 00:20:35,639
My roast chicken... Where did it go?

296
00:20:35,847 --> 00:20:36,932
Your Highness.

297
00:20:37,140 --> 00:20:38,099
My chicken!

298
00:20:39,434 --> 00:20:42,020
Your Highness, have you seen these men before?

299
00:20:46,858 --> 00:20:48,944
-Chief! -Tough luck, huh?

300
00:20:49,152 --> 00:20:49,986
Don't move.

301
00:20:50,987 --> 00:20:52,989
Drop your weapons and raise your hands.

302
00:21:01,414 --> 00:21:04,709
End of the line. Time to say your goodbyes.

303
00:21:07,712 --> 00:21:14,344
&lt;i&gt;Don't worry, Your Highness. If Ryotsu can just flip that switch...&lt;/i&gt;

304
00:21:14,678 --> 00:21:19,516
Not here. It's not here! Where's my roast chicken?!

305
00:21:20,016 --> 00:21:22,519
Where could it be? My roast chicken!

306
00:21:22,852 --> 00:21:25,981
He's probably still looking for that stupid roast chicken.

307
00:21:26,189 --> 00:21:27,232
Surely not...

308
00:21:27,440 --> 00:21:32,654
What are you whispering about? Saying your final prayers?

309
00:21:32,862 --> 00:21:35,031
You should be, because it's time to die!

310
00:21:36,700 --> 00:21:40,161
There it is! My roast chicken! Get in my belly!

311
00:21:54,467 --> 00:21:55,552
Yay!

312
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:57,012
Ryotsu!

313
00:21:57,595 --> 00:21:58,930
What just happened?

314
00:21:59,139 --> 00:22:02,267
Ryotsu activated the trapdoor switch.

315
00:22:02,475 --> 00:22:03,268
He did?

316
00:22:03,768 --> 00:22:07,897
My roast chicken... Where did it go?

317
00:22:11,943 --> 00:22:13,319
There it is!

318
00:22:14,738 --> 00:22:17,532
You did it, Ryo-chan! You're a hero!

319
00:22:17,741 --> 00:22:19,826
You saved our lives there.

320
00:22:20,034 --> 00:22:21,745
Thank you, Ryo-san!

321
00:22:23,121 --> 00:22:25,331
Oh, it was nothing.

322
00:22:29,586 --> 00:22:30,628
Huh? What's this?

323
00:22:31,671 --> 00:22:33,006
Oh no, that's...

324
00:22:37,218 --> 00:22:38,136
Take cover!

325
00:22:51,024 --> 00:22:54,360
He pushed the emergency self-destruct button.

326
00:22:56,029 --> 00:22:58,156
"POLICE HOSPITAL"

327
00:22:58,990 --> 00:23:01,284
Here, you deserve this award.

328
00:23:01,993 --> 00:23:03,661
You did great, Ryotsu.

329
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:05,955
Huh, I don't want that.

330
00:23:06,664 --> 00:23:12,128
I want that roast chicken! And sushi! I want the whole feast!

331
00:23:12,337 --> 00:23:16,299
Guess he's still upset at not getting to eat anything at the party.

332
00:23:16,925 --> 00:23:18,301
Here, for you.

333
00:23:19,135 --> 00:23:20,970
Huh? You?

334
00:23:21,179 --> 00:23:22,806
Thank you for saving my life.

335
00:23:23,014 --> 00:23:26,309
We had a right old laugh last night. So this is to thank you.

336
00:23:26,851 --> 00:23:28,520
Oh, Your Highness!

337
00:23:33,149 --> 00:23:34,818
You're too kind.

338
00:23:40,782 --> 00:23:43,076
Wasabi!

339
00:23:44,327 --> 00:23:45,703
You fell for it again!

340
00:23:45,912 --> 00:23:47,580
What a stupid gorilla!

341
00:23:47,789 --> 00:23:49,457
You damn brat!

342
00:23:53,795 --> 00:23:57,090
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

343
00:23:57,298 --> 00:24:02,011
ONE WING OF THE NAKAGAWA MANSION

344
00:24:05,473 --> 00:24:08,393
&lt;i&gt;Hey, guys! Kankichi Ryotsu is a genuine Tokyoite!&lt;/i&gt;

345
00:24:08,601 --> 00:24:11,354
&lt;i&gt;I'm always ready to fight fires, argue, or eat sushi!&lt;/i&gt;

346
00:24:11,563 --> 00:24:15,733
&lt;i&gt;No true Tokyoite would bathe in such lukewarm water! Heat this up, now!&lt;/i&gt;

347
00:24:16,860 --> 00:24:18,444
&lt;i&gt;You call this hot?&lt;/i&gt;

348
00:24:18,653 --> 00:24:20,572
NEXT EPISODE CLASH OF THE TOKYOITES!

349
00:24:20,780 --> 00:24:23,074
Don't miss it!

350
00:24:33,001 --> 00:24:37,297
&lt;i&gt;Let's keep smiling always&lt;/i&gt;

351
00:24:37,922 --> 00:24:41,551
&lt;i&gt;Even when things go wrong&lt;/i&gt;

352
00:24:41,759 --> 00:24:46,014
&lt;i&gt;Keep a pretty smile on your face&lt;/i&gt;

353
00:24:46,639 --> 00:24:51,102
&lt;i&gt;And go out as if nothing happened&lt;/i&gt;

354
00:24:51,644 --> 00:24:55,023
&lt;i&gt;Hey, show me your smile&lt;/i&gt;

355
00:24:55,231 --> 00:24:59,360
&lt;i&gt;You did nothing wrong&lt;/i&gt;

356
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:03,740
&lt;i&gt;Hey, show me your smile&lt;/i&gt;

357
00:25:03,948 --> 00:25:07,785
&lt;i&gt;Just like you did before, yeah&lt;/i&gt;

358
00:25:07,994 --> 00:25:12,123
&lt;i&gt;I want you to smile always&lt;/i&gt;

359
00:25:12,832 --> 00:25:17,295
&lt;i&gt;A woman with a frown isn't pretty&lt;/i&gt;

360
00:25:17,795 --> 00:25:23,343
&lt;i&gt;So you should smile as soon as you can&lt;/i&gt;

361
00:25:24,135 --> 00:25:27,096
&lt;i&gt;It's the grown-up thing to do&lt;/i&gt;

362
00:25:39,275 --> 00:25:44,072
KOCHIKAME SEE YOU NEXT TIME!
